WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
I swear there’s mountains over there somewhere.

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:03.999
Good morning, John.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.300
I’m going to Australia.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.360
Getting on the plane right now.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:10.260
I’m in Denver, or as I still honestly call
it, Isengard.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:11.360
Remember those, John?

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:18.180
Airports are a really good time to like sit and look at people,

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:24.120
and think, how do I feel like I know so much
that person just by glancing at them?

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:28.140
It feels like it takes so little data for
me to put somebody in a category.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.100
and then like, I also kind of believe it, though.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:34.080
Oh, that person’s a student. That person’s a businessperson. That’s just a family with kids.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.410
But it’s deeper than that, right?

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:39.180
‘Cause like, I look at somebody and I’ll
be like—I feel like I know things about them.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:44.680
I know things about their politics, or I know things about how they see the world, just by, like, looking at their beard.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.800
You can’t help but do that, right?

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.920
At least you gotta think about the fact that you’re doing it.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:51.420
This is my plane. They’re gonna put some food on it.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.820
Put some food on my plane, please.

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:56.570
My autofocus isn’t working, which is really—that’s not good.

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:00.220
This was an expensive lens. I want it to not be broken.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:05.520
I have great news: I turned it on and turned it back off again, and it works now.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.560
It jacked itself up. Now it’s up there. I didn’t expect that to happen.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:13.940
I mean, what’s in that thing, really? Except for just a bunch of pretzels.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.060
This makes me wanna play Airport Simulator.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.080
Okay, it’s 5:30, I am now playing Airport
Simulator at an airport.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.220
Getting on the plane.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:26.480
I’m in LA. This is what the ceiling looks like. I'm exhausted. Oh man.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:29.940
And there’s my gate. And there’s Dave’s head. Hello, Dave's head.

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:33.420
What’s that? Oh my God, this is a beautiful shot.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:34.560
Grace: Hi, Hank!

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.180
Hank: Grace just got really excited about
the US Open.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:39.600
Grace: Look, Lindsay Davenport is so excited! She’s crying! She’s so happy!

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.700
Hank: Who’s Lindsay Davenport?

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:45.940
Grace: Lindsay Davenport is a famous—like a—on the tail end of when Serena and Venus were like rising, she was like—

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:46.940
Hank: She’s a tennis player.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:49.880
Grace: Tennis player, yes. That’s the first thing I should have said. She’s a tennis player.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:53.780
The American underdog won, which is, like, what I wish the story of my life was.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:54.740
Getting on the plane.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:02:04.340
So the word is, stay up as late as you can,
and then go to sleep and wake up and it’ll be morning in Melbourne, so I’m just gonna power through. That's my plan.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:05.860
Everybody’s asleep.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:07.040
They say not to go to sleep.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:09.880
Why are all of these people going to sleep?

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:10.800
I guess I did have a coffee.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.180
The Earth is very big.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.600
I’m gonna work on some of my VidCon talks.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:16.560
I changed my mind.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.780
I’m watching One Punch Man.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.680
When I wake up, I’ll be in the southern
hemisphere.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.000
Is that painter’s tape?

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.100
Tiniest little toothpaste… Woah!

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:31.380
I frickin’ did it. I woke up a lot, but I just went back to bed.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:35.920
And when I woke up, pretty much everybody else had already woken up, so I feel like I win.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.000
I’m gonna have a great first day in Melbourne.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:56.080
This is my big, beautiful view of the outside of beautiful Melbourne,

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.480
and there’s a lot of beautiful sunlight coming through, and I got this chocolate bar.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.400
Oh no. Hello, beautiful chocolate. I’m sorry.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:08.080
I just got directions to boba tea from a Crash Course fan. We’ll see how this turns out.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.040
Success!

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:10.420
Cash only.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:12.860
More bad news. Okay, well, tomorrow, then.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.200
I rented a bike.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.200
This is where VidCon’s gonna be tomorrow.

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:23.880
It’s time now for something that I wanna do even though it seems a little silly.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.620
This looks like an okay spot.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:29.180
Southern hemisphere.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:40.520
John, I’ll see you on Tuesday.

